# Mermaid Runtime — agent standards

**Canonical copy:** [`AGENTS.md`](../../AGENTS.md). Cursor reads it directly; this rule makes sure it's applied every time. Don't copy its content here.

Before editing:

1. Read [`AGENTS.md`](../../AGENTS.md) and the session ledger in [`docs/runbook/00_index.md`](../../docs/runbook/00_index.md).
2. Read [`docs/agent-standards.md`](../../docs/agent-standards.md) (naming, JSDoc, terms) and [`docs/angular-standards.md`](../../docs/angular-standards.md).
3. Record findings in the runbook and update plan status as `AGENTS.md` describes. Add a ledger row before finishing.

Never stash, reset, restore, clean or force-push: other agents share this working tree.
